From: linhaifeng <522025320099@smail.nju.edu.cn>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 08:28:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] [PD][Kimi-K3][DSpark][1/N] Support speculative decoding
 with pooled KDA state (#1711)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

* feat(kimi-k3): support pooled speculative KDA checkpoints

outline:
- PR role — behavior: enable DSpark verification with pooled KDA state.

modify:
- Gather checkpoint blocks into a dense window and scatter all updated states back.
- Forward speculative metadata and cover BF16 and FP8 checkpoint rollback.
- Remove window-only activation rounding; leave existing dispatch guards unchanged.

reason:
- Problem: pooled KDA previously rejected speculative decoding.
- Design: reuse the dense kernel while preserving checkpoint addressing and untouched tails.

Signed-off-by: linhaifeng-nju <230823146+linhaifeng-nju@users.noreply.github.com>

* test(kda): cover invalid pooled speculative metadata

outline:
- PR role — verification: cover the pooled verify metadata rejection contract.

modify:
- Add seven CPU-eligible cases for missing offsets or checkpoints and invalid checkpoint request, window, or rank shapes.
- Assert the specific ValueError before pool access and kernel dispatch.
- Scope boundary: production code and numerical tolerances remain unchanged.

reason:
- Problem: successful checkpoint tests did not exercise existing metadata guards.
- Design: parameterized negative cases protect early failure without requiring TPU execution.

Signed-off-by: linhaifeng-nju <230823146+linhaifeng-nju@users.noreply.github.com>

